    <h1>About STEM Simulators</h1>
    <p><strong>STEMSimulators.org</strong> provides free, interactive, browser-based science visualizations and self-checking practice modules designed specifically for students, educators, and lifelong learners.</p>
    <p>Our mission is to make abstract scientific concepts—such as chemical reaction mechanisms and atomic electron configurations—intuitive through real-time visual experimentation, interactive drills, and instant feedback without requiring downloads or complex software installations.</p>
    <p>Whether used in a classroom laboratory or for independent review at home, these tools bridge the gap between static textbook problem sets and active digital exploration.</p>
